{"profile":{"name":"Neethan Shan","ward":"Ward 25, Scarborough—Rouge Park","bio":"Neethan Shan was elected to Toronto City Council in a by-election on September 29, 2025, succeeding Jennifer McKelvie, who resigned mid-term on May 9, 2025 after being elected to the House of Commons. He previously served as Toronto's first Tamil-Canadian city councillor for Ward 42 Scarborough—Rouge River from 2017 to 2018, and as a Toronto District School Board trustee (2016–2017 and 2022–2025, serving as Board Chair from 2024 to 2025). Born in Jaffna, Sri Lanka, he arrived in Canada as a refugee at age 16 and previously worked as a teacher, youth outreach worker, and executive director of the Urban Alliance on Race Relations.","committees":["Economic and Community Development Committee","Toronto Zoo Board of Management","Toronto and Region Conservation Authority Board of Directors","Scarborough Community Council"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_shan@toronto.ca","phone":"416-338-3771"},"promises":[{"text":"Fight for the transit Scarborough needs and support a regional transit plan specific to Scarborough.","source":"https://cliffcrestscarboroughvillagesw.ca/data/documents/2025-Rouge-Ward-25-By-election-Flashcard-FINAL.pdf?fbclid=IwY2xjawNC3PJleHRuA2FlbQIxMQABHmEMxkFWQImqozPI6jiIUdA-ACoPskfDndkzCt9k56EEuIfAXuI2AUHuXoib_aem_Vvha18E01A5rQ4haCwt7Yw"},{"text":"Ensure community voices are heard at City Hall and that neighbourhood associations play a key role in development decisions affecting their communities.","source":"https://cliffcrestscarboroughvillagesw.ca/data/documents/2025-Rouge-Ward-25-By-election-Flashcard-FINAL.pdf?fbclid=IwY2xjawNC3PJleHRuA2FlbQIxMQABHmEMxkFWQImqozPI6jiIUdA-ACoPskfDndkzCt9k56EEuIfAXuI2AUHuXoib_aem_Vvha18E01A5rQ4haCwt7Yw"},{"text":"Protect local businesses displaced by development and ensure local city projects support local businesses and create local jobs.","source":"https://cliffcrestscarboroughvillagesw.ca/data/documents/2025-Rouge-Ward-25-By-election-Flas